## Phase 13: CssValue Subclass Specialization
Introduce specialized `CssValue` subclasses to eliminate boxing, reduce allocations, and improve type safety for common value types. Follow the pattern established by `CssEnumValue<T>`.

### 13.1 CssListValue (COLLECTION) — High Priority ✓
Lists are extremely common: `font-family`, `background`, `transition`, `transform`, `box-shadow`, etc.
- [x] Create `CssListValue` subclass with direct `CssValue[]` storage
- [x] Add `ReadOnlySpan<CssValue> Values` property for allocation-free iteration
- [x] Add indexer `this[int index]` and `Count` property
- [x] Override `AsCollection()` to return existing array wrapped (or direct span access)
- [x] Override `TryFormat()` for space/comma-separated serialization
- [x] Override `Serialize()`, `Equals()`, `GetHashCode()`, `HasValue`
- [x] Support separator metadata (space vs comma-separated)
- [x] Update `CssValue.From(params CssValue[])` to return `CssListValue`
- [x] Add tests for CssListValue
- [x] Fixed `CssValue.Serialize()` bug for CSS-wide keywords (AUTO, INHERIT, etc.)

### 13.2 CssStringValue (STRING) — Medium Priority ✓
Strings are common in custom properties, `content`, quoted `font-family` names.
- [x] Create `CssStringValue` subclass with direct `string` storage
- [x] Override `AsString()` for direct access (no cast)
- [x] Override `TryFormat()` with proper CSS string escaping/quoting
- [x] Override `Serialize()`, `Equals()`, `GetHashCode()`, `HasValue`
- [x] Update `CssValue.From_String()` to return `CssStringValue`
- [x] Add tests for CssStringValue
- [x] Made `CssValue.AsString()` virtual to allow override

### 13.3 CssUrlValue (URL) — Low Priority ✓
- [x] Create `CssUrlValue` subclass with direct `CssUrl` storage
- [x] Override `AsUrl()` for direct access
- [x] Override serialization methods
- [x] Update `CssValue.From_Url()` to return `CssUrlValue`
- [x] Add tests for CssUrlValue
- [x] Made `CssValue.AsUrl()` virtual to allow override
- [x] Fixed bug in `CssUrl.TryFormat()` closing quote order

### 13.4 CssCalcValue (CALC) — Low Priority ✓
- [x] Create `CssCalcValue` subclass with direct `CssCalcExpression` storage
- [x] Override `AsCalcExpression()` for direct access
- [x] Override serialization methods
- [x] Update factory method to return `CssCalcValue`
- [x] Add tests for CssCalcValue
- [x] Made `CssValue.AsCalcExpression()` virtual to allow override

### 13.5 CssFunctionValue (FUNCTION) — Low Priority ✓
- [x] Create `CssFunctionValue` subclass with direct `CssFunction` storage
- [x] Override serialization methods for function syntax
- [x] Update factory method to return `CssFunctionValue`
- [x] Add tests for CssFunctionValue
- [x] Changed constructor to factory method `CssValue.From(CssFunction)`

### 13.6 Cleanup & Optimization
- [x] Audit remaining `data.ObjectValue` usages for potential subclass candidates
  - Created `CssVarValue` for VAR type (CssVarFunction storage)
  - Created `CssEnvValue` for ENV type (CssEnvFunction storage)
  - Created `CssUnicodeRangeValue` for UNICODE_RANGE type (CssUnicodeRange storage)
  - All ObjectValue-based types now have specialized subclasses
- [x] Consider sealing base `CssValue` class or making constructor internal-only
  - Changed `protected` constructor to `private protected` to prevent external subclassing
  - All existing subclasses are `sealed` within the assembly
  - External code must use factory methods (`From()`, etc.)
- [-] Update documentation with subclass usage patterns - Not Applicable
- [-] Performance benchmarks comparing old vs new implementations - Irrelevant

